cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "Please cite the relevant theorem paper and computational specification, and cite the underlying arithmetic sources separately."
type: software
title: "Polynomial presentations of the integers over the rationals"
authors:
  - name: "JUVa"
repository-code: "https://github.com/JoseBrox/diophantine-z-q_improvements"
url: "https://github.com/JoseBrox/diophantine-z-q_improvements"
date-released: 2026-11-14
version: "2026.11.14-v27"
license: CC-BY-4.0
abstract: >-
  Mathematical proofs and exact computational specifications for polynomial
  presentations of the integers over the rationals, under explicitly stated
  arithmetic premises. Current constructions use 25 variables with degree
  below 2^78, or 204 variables with exact degree four. Fully specified variants
  use 27 variables with degree below 2^80 and coefficient height below
  2^(2^92), or 260 quartic variables with height 149^38730+1 at N=9682.
  Additional weak abc hypotheses give 13 variables with degree below 2^38.
  Ordinary rational abc and the stated simultaneous-twist input of Jaswal
  give 79 quartic variables; a lower-coefficient 81-variable alternative is
  retained. Every count includes the input. The non-explicit defining
  thresholds remain ineffective. Exact computations and complete proofs of
  the new transformations are separate from the unfinished independent audit
  of the inherited arithmetic foundations. Supporting results include
  guarded finite-algebra elimination, positive weighted elliptic trace
  heights, complete reciprocal point charts, contact-height estimates and
  local obstructions. The v27 reference chart corrects an omitted term in
  the previous printed coefficient table.
keywords:
  - Diophantine definitions
  - Hilbert's tenth problem
  - rational points
  - explicit polynomials
  - elliptic heights
  - finite algebraic elimination
  - number fields
